      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to introduce to the market 5 Shrewsbury Lawn, an exceptional semi detached family home, occupying a prime position within this well established, mature residential locality. Offering incredible space, with four well proportioned bedrooms, this will appeal to growing families, with beautifully presented interiors presenting a turn key option for discerning buyers. \n\nThe property is approached by a cobblelocked drive with off street parking and a well manicured front lawn with mature plants and hedging. On entering the composite hall door the quality of finish within the home is immediately evident, with a wide, well lit entrance hall with wood flooring and modern, neutral colour schemes from the start. To the left you enter into the main living room, with a stone fireplace and fitted stove creating the focal point to this comfortable reception. There are double doors to the dining area, which opens out to the kitchen and has fitted units and integrated appliances, with a tiled floor which continues through to the adjacent utility room. There is a ground floor WC off the utility and access to the rear garden. Back into the kitchen, sliding doors lead to a sun room with glazing to two sides overlooking the rear garden. There is a further reception room towards the front of the property, opposite the living room, which is ideal for a family room, playroom or office. Upstairs there are four spacious bedrooms. The main bedroom offers plenty of wardrobe space, with fitted wardrobes and drawers, as well as a superb, modern ensuite shower room. A large, fully tiled shower room with walk in shower/wet room with modern, white suite sanitary ware completes the upstairs accommodation. \n\nOutside the gardens are immaculate and create a wonderful outdoor space, which is both private and accessible, with a gate to the rear which accesses a laneway. There is gated side access to the front and the rear garden is completely enclosed and ideal for young children or pets to play safely. There is a mix of lawn and patio, with mature trees and plants which makes a lush and secluded area. \n\nThe location could not be more convenient, ideally positioned within this mature cul-de-sac of similar homes, facing onto a green and set back from the Westbury exit road. There are numerous shops and eateries, as well as two supermarkets just minutes from the house across the other side of the Corbally Road, while the city centre is a short commute with bus routes practically on the doorstep. There are a number of educational facilities within walking distance including Scoil Ide Primary School and St Munchin's College, Corbally, whilst the University of Limerick is also easily accessible. A short drive north out of the city takes you into open countryside with numerous walks and beauty spots. Viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation: \nEntrance hall, living room, kitchen dining room, sunroom, utility, guest WC, family room, four bedrooms, ensuite shower room, family shower room/wet room. \nG.F.C.H."
      },
